The top delegate of the United Nations in Kabul has resigned.
The United Nations top delegate in Afghanistan, Kai Eide, said on Friday that he would like to resign from his post in March, ending a tumultuouous tenure, which has been thwarted by allegations of widespread corruption in the U.N.-backeded president's election in Afghanistan.
Eide's departure is taking place because the Obama administration has decided to send an additional 30000 U.S. troops to Afghanistan.
