Defense Secretary Robert M. Gates said on Friday that world powers would soon impose "further significant sanctions" on Iran because of a lack of involvement in conversations about his nuclear ambitions.
Gates, who spoke to a group of about 300 U.S. troops in northern Iraq during a week-to-day trip around the areas where wars in Afghanistan and Iraq, downplayed the prospects of armed actions against the Islamic Republic.
