Endesa and Barcelona, with an electric car
The energy company Endesa, together with the Barcelona City Hall, founded the 'LIVE office'.
It is a project for the development and promotion of an electric vehicle in the capital of Catalonia.
LIVE' (Logistics for the introduction of electric vehicles) sets out and manages the travel plan for the introduction of electric vehicles in the city and ensures mobility agreements, will handle, coordinate and submit contributions, etc.
It will also develop the MOVELE project, promote electric cars, gather opinions and results of activities in the participating sectors.
Overall, the purpose is to promote this means of transport of the future.
3 'Electrical cities'
However, Barcelona is not the only city involved in the project to introduce electric cars in Spain.
Madrid and Sevilla will join the project, too.
These are the three cities chosen by the government under the MOVELE Plan to support the introduction of electric cars.
Energy company Endesa has already signed a framework contract with the Catalan government.
The purpose is to support research and technological development activities in the Catalan Autonomous Region.
This includes energy-related activities and, above all, energy efficiency.
This is not the only initiative involving Endesa when it comes to the promotion of electric cars.
The company is represented in European standardization teams and actively carries out a number of additional projects such as G4V, ELVIRE or CENIT VERDE.
Zapatero anticipates the 'quiet period' in the automotive industry.
Prime Minister José Luis Rodríguez Zapatero predicts that Spain's automotive industry, the state's main export sector, is awaiting a "quiet period."
In the Prime Minister's economic report for 2009, Zapatero summarised the measures that were introduced during the year to support the automotive sector.
“Without a Competitive Plan for the automotive sector, we would face a state of abandonment today, the closure of some of our major manufacturing companies.”
"Thanks to this plan and the wishes of individual brands to continue to operate in Spain in this highly competitive sector, a certain period of calm for this industry is expected in the future, which is our main export sector," he added.
In this sense, he pointed out that the competitive plan, which forms part of the Automotive Integrated Plan (PIA), identified 800 million for the projects of 19 manufacturers and 137 auxiliary firms, which mobilized an investment in excess of 3 billion euros.
The Prime Minister explained that this investment is intended for the development of new models, for the modernization of production and existing processes.
Zapatero also highlighted the government's support measures and mentioned the 2000E plan, which applies in cooperation with autonomous regions and automotive brands.
According to the president's statement, this plan allowed to reduce by 6% the average level of emissions for new vehicles sold on the Spanish market, and ensured a "significant increase in" registrations, specifically in November by "40 percent".
20,000 square meters of classic vehicles
In Madrid will be opened the first International Salon of Classic Vehicles, which is a space for meetings of professionals and amateurs from the world of engines.
This initiative will take place from 5 to 7 February 2010 in the Glass Pavilion of Madrid Casa de Campo.
It is an exhibition area with an area of 20 000 square meters, on which more than 200 domestic and foreign exhibitors will be represented.
Here you will find not only classic motorcycles and cars, but in ClassicAuto Madrid there will also be products of all types related to the world of engines.
Exhibitors in the pavilion will offer accessories, spare parts, components, textile accessories, accessories, publications, miniatures, etc.
Hundreds of products related to classic engines, real treats for collectors and curious people.
Among the companies involved will be:Clásicos de Mos and Good Old Times, car sales; Juan Lumbreras, restoration; Coupe-Francisco Pueche, car sales and renewal; or Cochera Clásicos, a specialized firm of Mercedes Benz.
Exterior Eligibility Tests
In addition, the commercial activity of this salon will be complemented by parallel activities: concentrating, sports performances, performances, presentations and auditions.
Eligibility tests will also be carried out for classic cars and motorcycles in an adapted out-of-shoulder circuit.
Mazda3 i-Stop: maintaining a sporty style
Mazda intends to show that environmental friendliness has no negative effect on sporty style.
And that’s why the Mazda3 has a built-in engine stop and start system – also baptized like-Stop-, a device that’s currently only available with a 2.0 150-horsepower gasoline engine.
This second generationMazda3 is characterized by the good characteristics it has achieved as a whole.
Surface treatment, vehicle design, habitability, behavior, mechanics, i-Stop...
All of these aspects are excellent at Mazda3.
The front seats, incl. the driver's seat, have excellent ergonomics and are perfectly fixed.
The steering wheel is also extremely fine.
Using the tool line-up and console, we conclude that Mazda continues Japan's tendency to develop futuristic design with many buttons and controls and a distinctive red and blue color.
This style partly reminds us of the style also presented by the Honda Civic.
Therefore, we can say that Mazda3 and Civic, both Japanese, contrast with the sobriety of German products and, more specifically, withVolkswagen Golf, which everyone wants to beat.
As is usual, this Japanese compact product represents more than enough space for four adults who want a very comfortable ride.
In addition, it is necessary to mention a large luggage compartment and regular shapes.
So far, the automatic stopping and start-up system is only available with a two-litre petrol engine and 150 horsepower with a six-speed manual transmission.
This engine is a real treat. It is very gentle, characterized by reduced noise levels, its performance and lower consumption.
Although Mazda3 is in the diesel version, all those who don’t drive so many kilometres per year shouldn’t rule out this i-Stop with a petrol engine because it’s characterized by greater driving comfort and reduced consumption.
In terms of equipment, the version selected for testing is called Sportive and includes a larger number of serial elements.
For serial equipment, it is necessary to mention in particular the lane monitoring system (RVM), which prevents the appearance of a blind spot, tension and stability control, speed control, interior mirror sensitive to light, on-board computer with large screen, parking sensors, separate air conditioning, rain and light sensor,bluetooth and bluetooth audio and wheels made of 17-inch alloy.
And if the equipment was not sufficient, this version was equipped withPack Premium, at an additional cost of 1,500 euros: adaptable two-xenon and sound system BOSE with CD holder, in addition to other components.
Conclusion
Mazda3 2.0 i-Stop is one of the most compact cars of its category.
It is characterized mainly by the quality of the materials used, its operation and high level of equipment.
Moreover, people who do not drive more kilometers per year can choose this i-Stop version, which is only with a gasoline engine2.0 and 150 hp.
The only disadvantage of this model is its higher price, which is21.770 euros for the Luxury version and 23.270 euros for the tested version -Sportive-.
At this high price, Mazda3 offers us a great deal of satisfaction for every day.
