Poker Manuela Vicenta
Manuel Vicent donates thirty X-rays of writers he has encountered in his literary life (and, in some cases, even in everyday life).
It does not do so in dreaded and predictable genres (biographical similarity, life and work), but is looking for something similar to the core of a creative personality.
The journey brings excitement, and Vicent doesn't spare shocks or inspiration.
This book is an excellent reading experience, even with repeated reading.
Here are some observations.
In the pages of this book I have found that the Mediterranean is not the sea, but the spiritual impulse, almost physical, the same as what I feel, but it cannot be named: the enjoyment of counter-destiny, morality without guilt and innocence without any god.”
About Samuel Beckett: "Nihilist, an allegorical Christian, wrote according to his own nature and not intellect, something between helplessness and ignorance, with blinding poetic humor, without meaning, as if it were the blade of the knife that almost killed him."
About Graham Green: "Our man has beent with a passion for this woman for thirteen years, adultery, pleasure and remorse, which is a spiritual privilege for reaching heaven by way of damnation."
About James Joyce: "This Odysseus was published by Sylvia Beach in Paris in 1922. It is one of the eight thousand peaks in universal literature, which must be overcome from the north side, from which the best climbers often collapse."
William Faulkner: "He was a weird man.
On his own, he said he was the heir to a landlord from the county, other times he was the son of a black woman with a crocodile.
In both cases, these were great dreams.”
About Louis-Ferdinand Céline: "This writer captured on the bridge a deranged cry of this man from Munich to bring his echo into the night of the 20th century in his literary form, running away from himself and calling for the future and speaking violently to the worms."
About Dorothy Parker: "Once she knelt down and prayed, 'My beloved God, make me stop writing like a woman.'
About Joseph Conrad: "Spenser's verses were engraved on his grave: 'After the effort the dream will come,/ after the storm a peaceful harbour,/after the war rest,/after a full-fledged life death."
About Virginia Wolf: "He's been carrying his depressions in his luggage, too.
The husband completely agreed to tell him that Edward VII was watching her among the azaleas or that the birds sang Greek.
Never before has any man been so patient and in love with a neurotic whose literary talent goes hand in hand with folly.”
About Pío Baroja: "What's Martín Santos's point other than to focus Joyce on the Barohea?
What's Benet's other than to have Baroi executed by Faulkner's weapon?
What else was it about Cell, other than to be made famous at the expense of the man's glory?"
Coward Aggression
Last week my seventy-year-old mother walked through our neighborhood in Fuenlabrada district, and a group of young people aged 15 to 18 passed by and our dog, a hybrid rescued from a shelter weighing a maximum of six kilograms, without a single word kicked him twice and badly injured him.
Our outrage is all the greater because we don't see anything funny about such aggression against a small and defenseless animal, which, moreover, was on a leash.
And on top of that, the old lady's shock after this incident, when she encountered these individuals on a walk, began to worry about her own safety, for such a devil-obsessed man who attacked an animal is able to do the same to a woman, a child, an old person or anyone who is weaker than himself.
It happened at five o'clock in the afternoon, on Tuesdays, in a usually quiet neighborhood.
The dog cried all day.
Of course, we have filed a complaint against the nearest commissary, but we doubt that it was for something, and in order not to raise delicate questions, we note that these coward killers were Spanish nationals.
Outrage prompted us to announce this fact.
We don't understand what's going on with today's youth when they're having fun worrying about a defenseless animal that's giving us love, society and friendship.
We don't understand where good manners have gone, respect for animals and people.
Michelin and Fesvial together for using helmets
In cooperation with the Spanish Transport Safety Foundation (Fesvial), tyre maker Michelin has launched a campaign to promote the use of helmets, especially for younger motorists, as both of them have reported today.
The purpose of this initiative is to emphasise the importance of using a helmet, since it is the only means by which it is possible to prevent head injuries or death in the event of a motorcycle accident.
Michelin states that this campaign forms part of their transport safety commitments, which "means more than designing and producing even safer products" and has confirmed that it is trying to fulfill this purpose, i.e. in the form of an instructional and information campaign.
This new campaign to promote the use of a helmet when riding a motorcycle, under the motto 'To be or not to be', is the first stage, when more than 500 motorcycle repairs will be deployed to become known to the widest public.
Finally, Michelin pointed out that transport safety "is a constant problem" of this company, which is a manufacturer of tires for two-wheeled vehicles and whose main goal is to constantly improve the safety of products.
The sale of light commercial vehicles is increasing
After almost two years, the market for light commercial vehicles is starting to recover.
All 9,425 vehicles registered in Spain recorded an increase of 12.6% in November compared to 2008 and what is more, this is the first increase after 22 months of permanent bankruptcy, according to the figures of the patronage organization of Anfac manufacturers and Ganvam dealers.
However, it is better to quarantine the favourable figure, as November 2008 is a very bad period for comparison and meant a 60% reduction compared to the previous year.
As a result, despite the increase in the last month, the total number of registered vehicles in the last 11 months accounts for 40% less than in the previous financial year.
As of January, 95,853 vehicles have been sold, which includes all possible vehicles falling into the category of light commercial vehicles: passenger car derivatives, pick-ups, deliveries, smaller trucks and light trucks/chassis.
And the glooms that are most damaging to demand, even when purchased by private individuals, most of the purchases were made by small and medium-sized companies, and in almost 100% of cases it is financing through third parties.
Other factors such as cessation of activity or the continuation of a bad economic situation should also be added to the constraints resulting from the closure of the source of bank loans.
In the given situation, unlike passenger cars, the support of buying the 2000E did not help much.
In addition to private individuals, it is necessary to mention persons operating on a trade license of a small and medium-sized company, which intend to purchase a light commercial vehicle up to 3.5 tons with CO2 emission levels not exceeding 160 grams per kilometre, but the number of operations has been confirmed.
Just yesterday from Ganvam, they reiterated the need to pay special attention to the management of these vehicles, as well as industrial vehicles (trucks and buses).
The Association of Dealers expects that in 2010 the development will be similar to last year and, according to calculations, sales for passenger cars and 4x4 will fall by 19%.
The auxiliary system at the handbrake is already mandatory equipment.
As in the case of the ABS anti-locking system, it will also be with ESP stability control, auxiliary handbrake systems, all of which will become the mandatory equipment of European cars.
In fact, it already forms part of the mandatory equipment of all newly registered passenger cars and light commercial vehicles, while for others, a deadline is set to eliminate shortages, which is February 2011.
The measures put in place in the EU aim to increase pedestrian protection, working to help prevent many collisions.
Auxiliary handbrake system increases the pressure on the brakes in an emergency case, which the system detects after the driver presses.
But it doesn't always sustain that pressure until the end.
According to a study conducted by automotive parts maker Bosch, one-third of drivers who have an accident did not push the brake before the collision, and half of them did not take full advantage of the brake force.
Up to 1,100 accidents
On the contrary, this assistance requires maximum from the braking system, shortens the braking distance of the vehicle.
According to a study carried out in the EU itself, if all vehicles were equipped with this type of equipment, up to 1,500 pedestrian-related fatal accidents could be avoided.
Reducing this number will be even more noticeable, according to calculations, would prevent one of four accidents with an impact on people-after the introduction of so-called intelligent handbrake systems.
In this case, the vehicles will be equipped with a system that (using radar or camera) captures obstacles and reports them to the driver, in addition to light braking.
If the driver reacts, it will help him increase the pressure on the pedal if needed.
If the driver does not respond, even if the collision cannot be prevented, the device impresses the brake as intensely as possible and reduces the risk of damage to a minimum.
