Reducing the weight does not mean that the vehicle does not press against asphalt.
Quite the contrary: for a long time we have not tested such a small and light model, which at the same time would transfer such safety when moving in the corner, even at high speeds.
He's a small athlete capable of warming the muscles during a short ride for the necessary time, until we've ordered him sprint, braking, and restoring the use of the engine...
Anything we're going to want. Thanks to steering that's as communicative as accurate, whatever we're hinting out with our hands on the steering wheel is what the car does.
And he'll do it with surgical precision.
The sound of the engine according to the clearance
The sound of the V6 boxer, about 320 hp (about 10 more than the Boxster S) is very successful and it is possible to enhance it with 'sport' options and through a system that modifies the sound of an engine that has previously been used at Panamera.
Acceleration capacity is brutal, whether during suction or recuperation.
Curtains are solid, but not hard or uncomfortable.
The asphalt of the roads we're passing through with Boxster Spyder was pretty damaged, but the car handled the potholes well.
Electronic support was almost unnecessary during the ride; and yet in some corners we came across at dawn on icing and gravel even on an advanced morning.
Definitely, this ultra-light car is one of the funniest on the market, as it’s a bit more than just a Boxster S modification.
The car will go on sale in February 2010 at a price70,831 euros.
