New tools for car valuation
In these days, storms and accidents not only make car repair shops.
Every day thousands of cars that have suffered an insured event are towed to service, where an expert has to estimate damages and repair costs.
No insured event is the same, and the calculation of the cost of parts and the time of the workforce can be long and complex work.
Calculating manually the repair costs from 20,000 to 30,000 euros including parts and workforce can take two or three hours.
However, with the support of new computer tools, it would be a matter of minutes
That's why almost 100% of experts use this kind of system.
Suppliers of services and solutions for estimating claims and maintenance are dedicated to collecting the information provided by manufacturers to then develop and offer their customers a useful tool.
In Spain Audatex, from the U.S. Solera Group is a leading company; 80% of the evaluation is carried out with its products.
Other firms competing in valuation tools and producing information about the sector are GtMotive and Eurotax.
Working with data provided by manufacturers is not easy at all.
According to Eduard Velázquez, Audatex's sales director, they work in Spain with 63 manufacturers and importers, and each provides them with information in a different format.
In addition, the amount of data for processing continues to grow, as more versions, variants and engine solutions have been introduced in the last five years than in the previous fifteen years.
Once a new vehicle enters the market, these businesses will start working.
It is a very fevery work, because it is necessary to catalog each of the thousands of parts of the vehicle and determine its price.
In addition, for each model, a "smart" graphical processing is carried out, where it is possible to "pickle out" the individual parts of tourist cars.
When it comes to a model with massive sales, the work can be done in a week if the process is very fast.
When it comes to a minority car, it can take three or four months. At present, Audatex has complete information on 99.2% of cars sold in Spain.
Among the most exclusive models they have information about are Porsche, but, for example, not Ferrari or Lamborghini.
It exceeds 99% in circulation with regard to a mobile park.
In order to carry out the work of documenting and elaborate databases, Audatex has eighter centers divided around the world (Spain, France, Germany, the USA, Brazil, Mexico, China and Japan) and each of them specializes in specific brands.
The national residence is in Alcobendas (Madrid).
There more than a hundred technicians (normally experts in mechanics) work together with three computer screens.
Audatex invests 90 million euros a year in the development of these databases.
2.5 million data is included each month, and customers receive updates every two days.
The processing of this enormous stream of information allows businesses to make different uses and provision of different products.
The most common use focuses on repair and maintenance, but by country there are also tools for managing spare parts or for calculating the sales or residual value of a car.
The only undertaking to have a guide that informs about the value of used vehicles in Spain is Eurotax.
Audatex doesn't offer them in our country, but in the United States, yes.
Taking into account the products offered by Audatex, it’s easy to get support that can be enjoyed by sector professionals.
This business offers ten different tools, with AudaPlus, a standallor insurance valuation solution designed for connoisseurs.
It includes cars, motorcycles and light and heavy industrial vehicles.
In addition to the cost of parts, it also includes repair time estimated by the manufacturer or paint shop.
This tool is paid according to use for each evaluation.
The highest price is 5.75 euros for customers who use it little, a maximum of ten times a month.
After that, each insurance company that makes thousands of estimates will negotiate its price with Audatex.
Other products such as AudaVIN allow for full identification of the vehicle and the equipment with which it came out of the assembly line only on the basis of the first chassis number.
AudaGlass focuses on vehicle glasses and AudaSubastas is an open service to the professional sector on the Internet, which allows you to decommission vehicles with an overall insured event.
Its statistical service is very useful for the identification of tendencies, performing geodemographic analyses or detecting deviations by brands or models.
For example, it is possible to study how many model-to-certainous brands have undergone service due to a crash or how many have suffered serious insurance claims over a particular period.
Gt Motive is the only Spanish company dedicated to the development of this type of tools.
Among other things, it sells Gt Estimate, which is also intended for connoisseurs, as well as providing digital images, access to parts or prices, and the manufacturer's official times.
Gt Motive is an Einsa company founded in 1971 as a supplier of services and solutions for damage assessments, accidents or car maintenance
Gt Guía valuation is its reference historical product on the market.
They work with 24,000 users in services, 3.100 experts and 53 insurance companies.
The turnover volume increased by 20% per year over the last three years and charged 10.8 million euros in 2008.
At the beginning of last year, the process of internationalization by installing an office in Paris began.
Audatex was founded in Germany in 1966 and established itself in Spain in 1979.
According to the company's sources, 62% of its broths arise in Europe and 38% in North and South America. It works with 900 insurance companies and 33,000 services, including 3,000 in Spain.
Solera (Audatex, Sidexa, Informex ABZ, Hollander and IMS) will reach US$557 million, which is 3.3% more than in 2008.
In our country, the company earns 19.1 million euros, which is 7.2% more than last year.
In 2005, Solera stood at €1,000 million on the stock exchange, and its shares are now estimated at a total value of US$2,400 million.
It has been listed on the New York Stock Exchange since 2007 and is included in the Standard & Poor's reference index.
Internet auction of crashed vehicles
Last October, Solera Group bought Autoonline, an internet base for the sale of cars and motorcycles or special vehicles after an insurance event.
The operation projected 59.5 million euros out of 85% of the company's capital, which could be expanded next year by the remaining 15%.
The aim of the purchase was to provide more value-added services to customers with the possibility of access to a huge international market.
This valuation and purchase and sales service is guaranteed exclusively to professionals in the sector, such as insurance companies, connoisseurs, rental companies, services, spare parts sales and professional dealers who have to register before operations begin.
This platform was established in 1996 in Germany and manages more than 650,000 operations across Europe, including 500,000 in Germany.
Spain, Greece, Poland and Turkey stand out among the main markets.
The website currently has more than 1,500 registered vendors and 4,000 experts.
It manages 3,000 daily adverts, and about 100 new adverts are added to the Spanish market every day.
Under Spanish law, a car whose chassis number has been decommissioned cannot return to service, but it can be used as a source of spare parts that have not been damaged.
Vehicles with a historical value may be allowed to operate, even if they have been decommissioned, after preliminary proceedings.
Service budget in four steps
With Auda-Taller, Audatex guarantees that the user will only get a budget in four steps: identifying the vehicle, finding a spare part, creating a budget generation budget.
The ease of use is an essential condition for these systems, especially for the beliefs of older-age professionals, who, to a greater or lesser extent, are restrained in the use of new management techniques.
The database contains 1.034 vehicles, of which 666, 109 off-road, 137 motorcycles, 78 vans and 44 trucks.
Naturally for use, you need a computer with an internet connection.
After identifying the model to be repaired, using the chassis number, a real graphical display of the model appears, and then the necessary spare part is selected.
The user can include variables such as workforce price, surcharges or discounts, and then print and pass to the customer.
AudaTaller is not a valuation tool like AudaPlus, but rather a reference catalogue.
The main difference between the two systems is that it is service-oriented and does not include an estimate of the workforce.
The cost of using this tool for the workshop is 350 euros a year, which the customer can finance.
Currently Audatex is working to make these views three-dimensional.
This is an innovation that mechanics welcome, for example, because it will allow, for example, to select the door and turn it to display the inside.
